course: dictionary
lesson: 14848
title: Words for people and places
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word ending in -er often names a person who does a job. A baker bakes bread, and a rancher runs a ranch. «The rancher checked the cattle every morning.» The sentence tells you the rancher looks after animals, so a rancher is someone who owns or runs a ranch.
explain: A ranch is a very large farm, mostly in the USA, Canada and Australia. The animals are often cattle, sheep or horses, and they graze on wide grasslands. «My cousin is a sheep rancher in Australia.» The word before rancher, sheep, tells you which animals this rancher keeps.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. Does «The farmer checked the cattle every morning» still make sense? Yes, so you are close. But a ranch is much bigger than an ordinary farm, and the dictionary tells you that. Context and the dictionary together give you the full meaning.
fact: A rancher owns or runs a ranch.
fact: A ranch is a very large farm where cattle, sheep or horses are raised.
fact: Ranches are mainly found in the USA, Canada and Australia.
fact: «Cattle rancher» means a rancher who raises cows and bulls.
fact: In the USA, a ranch-style house is a long, low house on one floor. This is a different meaning of ranch, not a farm.
exercise: «The rancher rode across the grassland on her horse.» Who is the rancher? | A kind of cloud | *A person who owns or runs a large farm | A town in the desert | A horse that carries riders
exercise: «My cousin is a sheep rancher in Australia.» What does a sheep rancher raise? | Fish | *Sheep | Bees | Pigeons
exercise: Ella says, «A ranch is a small shop that sells cattle.» Is Ella right? | Yes, but only in the USA | Yes, a ranch is a small shop | *No, a ranch is a very large farm | No, a ranch is a school for horses
test: In old westerns, what do ranchers often do? | *Ride horses and drive cattle | Sail across the sea | Bake bread for the town | Sing in a choir
test: «Maria is a rancher in Canada.» Where does Maria work? | In a hospital | In a school | *On a large farm called a ranch | In a shop by the sea
exam: Tom says, «My aunt is a rancher in Texas.» Which meaning fits best? | A teacher who gives riding lessons | *A person who owns or runs a large farm called a ranch | A person who cooks food in a café | A person who builds houses for a living
